1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:04,000
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:33,800
[both growling]

3
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:36,350
I suppose...

4
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,720
I'll give this one a try.

5
00:01:38,810 --> 00:01:41,230
[both growling]

6
00:01:46,650 --> 00:01:48,820
Way off! This'll take
some adjustment!

7
00:01:51,650 --> 00:01:52,570
[thudding]

8
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:54,280
Gabby.

9
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,280
Are there any assailants
in your area?

10
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:58,830
[GABBY] Yeah,
something came at me.

11
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:02,710
When did these freaks
manage to get inside the manor?

12
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:04,790
Guess you're dealing
with some guys of your own?

13
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,130
[JIN] Yeah, we're dealing
with a pair as we speak.

14
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:09,170
[grunts]

15
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:10,960
[GABBY] Well,
take care of 'em already.

16
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:13,010
[JIN] I'm trying,
but with limited mobility.

17
00:02:13,090 --> 00:02:15,680
Huh? Don't give me that crap!

18
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,180
Don't you have
Asa there with you?

19
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:18,600
You'd better protect her!

20
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:21,140
[JIN] We have Yuru
and his daemons.

21
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,390
They're helping.

22
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,730
[GABBY] Those guys
who knocked my teeth in?

23
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:26,980
[grunts] Dumb bastards.
You'll be fine then.

24
00:02:27,810 --> 00:02:30,150
You mind if I just
do my thing over here?

25
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,320
[JIN] Be my guest.

26
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:34,400
Thank you.

27
00:02:34,490 --> 00:02:36,110
[grunts]

28
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:38,490
Gobble.

29
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:44,250
[screeches]

30
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:48,210
[GABBY] What to do?

31
00:02:48,290 --> 00:02:50,210
It would just be so cruel
to leave you

32
00:02:50,290 --> 00:02:52,250
-alone without your other half.
-[whimpers]

33
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,380
Gobble.

34
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:55,840
[whimpers]

35
00:03:06,270 --> 00:03:07,400
[Gabby smirks]

36
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,530
Aren't you lucky, Gabriel?

37
00:03:12,610 --> 00:03:14,490
You get a midnight snack!

38
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:17,700
It seems Miss Gabby
is managing all right.

39
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:20,570
Thank goodness.
Now how about I stop them?

40
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:22,910
[YURU] You can do that?

41
00:03:22,990 --> 00:03:24,160
[ASA] If I do, can I hug you?

42
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:26,460
You're so big
you'd break my ribs.

43
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:29,670
Hey, Jin. Sorry if I make
a mess of this place.

44
00:03:29,750 --> 00:03:31,670
I'll take the heat
from the old man.

45
00:03:31,750 --> 00:03:33,250
Do whatever you have to.

46
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:37,430
Hey, Jin, I'm also sorry
if I make a mess of this place!

47
00:03:37,510 --> 00:03:39,340
[JIN] You're gonna have
to take the heat yourself.

48
00:03:39,430 --> 00:03:41,890
[HARUO] What a blatant
double standard!

49
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:45,640
Give me a hand!

50
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:47,810
Brother, go ahead
and distract the white one!

51
00:03:47,890 --> 00:03:49,270
Don't give me orders.

52
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:50,350
But I'm on it.

53
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:54,190
[both growling]

54
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:01,820
[Asa gasps]

55
00:04:02,830 --> 00:04:03,780
[Yuru gasps]

56
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:09,670
Where'd she go?

57
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:10,830
Asa?

58
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,340
[JIN] She vanished.

59
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:17,010
And Yuru, too?
What is this thing?

60
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:19,300
Stop it!

61
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:25,760
[HARUO] I don't know
what they did,

62
00:04:25,850 --> 00:04:28,390
but it seems like they make
people disappear.

63
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,520
So there's a chance
these guys are the ones

64
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,190
who kidnapped Asa's parents!

65
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:39,110
[JIN] The damage
to the floorboards is fine,

66
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:40,530
but no killing.

67
00:04:40,610 --> 00:04:41,990
Them or their master.

68
00:04:42,070 --> 00:04:43,410
[HARUO] Got it, boss man.

69
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:46,950
Haruo, there are enemy daemons
on all sides!

70
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:47,950
[HARUO] Uh?

71
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,830
I'm needed here!
It's all you, Jin!

72
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:52,080
[JIN] What?

73
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:54,710
[BUNBUN] Me too! Haruo needs
his bodyguard!

74
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:55,920
[JIN] Really?

75
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:59,380
[Jin groans]
Why's it gotta happen

76
00:04:59,470 --> 00:05:02,640
when the master Natsuki
and Fuyuki are all out?

77
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,430
So, where's Hagure?

78
00:05:04,510 --> 00:05:07,010
[SAKURAZAWA]
Sleeping after a tight deadline.

79
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,980
Wake him,
and it'll be your head.

80
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:10,480
[Jin sighs]

81
00:05:13,650 --> 00:05:15,650
[JIN] No reinforcements then.

82
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,990
Well, my friends,
let's get to work.

83
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,740
Late night, long shift.

84
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:26,330
[ASA] Big Brother! Yuru!
[echoes]

85
00:05:26,410 --> 00:05:29,580
Hey, Jin? Or Haruo?

86
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:31,540
Or Doctor Sakurazawa?

87
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,170
Hey, Ai?

88
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,630
Makoto?

89
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:35,920
Torty, maybe?

90
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,340
Or Bunbun?

91
00:05:38,250 --> 00:05:40,420
[Asa sighs]

92
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:44,800
I'm all alone.

93
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:48,680
[Asa breathes shakily]

94
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:53,350
[Asa whimpers]

95
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:59,150
You're not as alone
as you think you are!

96
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:00,530
[Asa screams]

97
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,780
My brother's daemon?

98
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:04,740
[RIGHT] Yeah,
but you can call me Right.

99
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:07,700
It's too dark in here
to see you.

100
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:11,450
[RIGHT] I'm out of luck too.
But rest assured, I'm nearby.

101
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:14,750
You know,
this is serious darkness.

102
00:06:14,830 --> 00:06:17,000
Even Higashi Village
in the dead of night

103
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,630
can't compare.

104
00:06:18,710 --> 00:06:20,750
Can't see my own hand. Hm?

105
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,760
You reek
of cold sweat, lass.

106
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,640
Are you afraid of the dark?

107
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,720
♪

108
00:06:33,350 --> 00:06:34,890
[ASA] Not always.

109
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:37,560
Just... when I'm alone.

110
00:06:38,730 --> 00:06:41,480
[RIGHT] Your scent
is coming from this way.

111
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:44,990
Don't fret, lass.
I'm right by your side.

112
00:06:45,070 --> 00:06:47,280
I'm not gonna leave you
to fend for yourself.

113
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,580
[Asa sighs softly]

114
00:06:50,370 --> 00:06:52,200
[Asa yelps] Where's my brother?

115
00:06:52,290 --> 00:06:53,660
Is Yuru here?

116
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:56,000
You would be able to tell
if he were, would you not?

117
00:06:56,630 --> 00:06:58,290
Doesn't smell like
he's stuck in this place.

118
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:00,840
Aren't you contracted
to take care of him?

119
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,840
Why aren't you rushing
straight to his side?

120
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:06,090
He's got Left, so I can't say
I'm too concerned.

121
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:07,890
They'll figure something out.

122
00:07:07,970 --> 00:07:10,310
I followed you because
I thought we should chat.

123
00:07:10,390 --> 00:07:11,970
Or are you busy right now?

124
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:13,390
What do you want?

125
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:16,690
[RIGHT] You fired at me
when we first met.

126
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,310
A blast of energy
straight out of your hand.

127
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:23,070
And you haven't been much warmer
since I came to this manor.

128
00:07:23,150 --> 00:07:25,820
You didn't see fit to offer me
a simple hello?

129
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:30,370
Or maybe you already realized
that I'm your enemy.

130
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:34,080
[Asa grunts softly]

131
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:37,370
[ASA] Back then,
when you countered...

132
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:40,210
Or... No... Maybe canceled?

133
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:42,000
What did I do?

134
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:45,460
[ASA] I'm sorry.
It's hard to describe.

135
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,180
Neutralized?

136
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:50,970
Yeah, when you
neutralized Break,

137
00:07:51,050 --> 00:07:53,100
something my father said
came back to me.

138
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:56,310
He said Left and Right
are guardians.

139
00:07:56,390 --> 00:07:58,350
They're to keep Break and Seal

140
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:00,110
from ever getting
out of control.

141
00:08:00,190 --> 00:08:03,020
That makes this talk
easy for me!

142
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,530
As the wielder of Break,
you're my nemesis.

143
00:08:06,610 --> 00:08:09,360
Nice to meet you, Asa.

144
00:08:09,450 --> 00:08:10,870
[ASA] On the other hand,

145
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:13,660
if my brother acquires
the power of Seal,

146
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:15,910
she'll be his nemesis, too.

147
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:18,960
Such is the natural order
of things, I suppose.

148
00:08:21,420 --> 00:08:24,300
[yelps] You're here too, Left?

149
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:27,420
Aye, in this void.
An odd place.

150
00:08:28,050 --> 00:08:30,630
Yeah, just where are we?

151
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:33,970
No idea. I've lived
many a lifetime and more,

152
00:08:34,050 --> 00:08:36,060
and yet this is still new.

153
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:38,100
How strange.

154
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:39,520
There is ground.

155
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:42,560
But all of this white
is distorting my perception.

156
00:08:42,650 --> 00:08:46,230
While flying, I found... a roof?
Or something like?

157
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:47,780
It seems we are closed in.

158
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,860
I cannot be certain,

159
00:08:49,950 --> 00:08:52,320
but it appears we're inside
a spherical barrier

160
00:08:52,410 --> 00:08:54,450
made by the daemon pair
from before.

161
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:56,700
We're trapped in a barrier?

162
00:08:56,790 --> 00:08:57,910
[Yuru grunts]

163
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:01,370
[YURU] Are there
any enemies around?

164
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:02,920
[LEFT] Far as I can tell,

165
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,090
there is naught else here
but us.

166
00:09:05,790 --> 00:09:08,920
All right, then I would like
some help adjusting to this bow.

167
00:09:09,010 --> 00:09:11,550
-You mind?
-Is now the right time?

168
00:09:11,630 --> 00:09:13,470
I've got no clue
what's going on,

169
00:09:13,550 --> 00:09:15,930
but I don't want
to just stand around.

170
00:09:16,010 --> 00:09:18,770
My father taught me to keep
my tools in good condition.

171
00:09:18,850 --> 00:09:20,640
And to be ready
for a fight anywhere

172
00:09:20,730 --> 00:09:22,390
with whatever
I've got on hand.

173
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:24,980
Does being
in such an unfamiliar situation

174
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:26,650
hold no fear for you?

175
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:28,320
Why should I fear anymore?

176
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:30,110
It's been the same every day.

177
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:32,740
Nothing has made sense
since the village was attacked.

178
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:34,200
Why would I feel afraid

179
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:37,410
when being confused
has become so normal to me?

180
00:09:37,490 --> 00:09:39,200
-[Yuru chuckles]
-[LEFT] Poor lad.

181
00:09:39,290 --> 00:09:40,710
♪

182
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:46,460
[YURU] Stand there and raise
the billhook high.

183
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:48,170
That's my target.

184
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:49,380
[LEFT] Like this?

185
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:50,550
[YURU] Perfect.

186
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,520
Don't just let it hit you!

187
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,890
[LEFT]
Retrieving the arrows later

188
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:04,270
would be obnoxious
if I were to dodge them now.

189
00:10:04,350 --> 00:10:05,980
[YURU] Yeah, but come on!

190
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:07,570
No reason to worry.

191
00:10:07,650 --> 00:10:09,900
As I told you,
I'm sculpted of stone.

192
00:10:11,950 --> 00:10:13,280
[YURU] I am so sorry!

193
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:15,950
Hey, are these on straight?

194
00:10:16,030 --> 00:10:18,620
[LEFT] Are you not concerned
for your sister's well-being?

195
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,700
[YURU] Huh? What for?

196
00:10:20,790 --> 00:10:22,120
[LEFT] As we are trapped here,

197
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:25,000
she was swallowed by
the black daemon's barrier.

198
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,170
Well, yeah. But she's got
that Break thing.

199
00:10:28,790 --> 00:10:32,260
If they really are barriers,
I figure she'll be fine.

200
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:34,800
[both growling]

201
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:40,310
What, Torty?

202
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:46,560
[grunting]

203
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:48,900
[ASA] We're out!

204
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:52,240
Aye! So, the barrier
was inside this daemon!

205
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:54,900
-[Haruo exclaims]
-Glad you're back, Asa!

206
00:10:54,990 --> 00:10:56,530
Thanks, Bunbun!

207
00:10:57,410 --> 00:10:58,660
As for you...

208
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:03,160
I'm going to take your contract
with your master and Break it!

209
00:11:05,580 --> 00:11:07,580
[grunting]

210
00:11:12,550 --> 00:11:14,220
[SAKURAZAWA] Heads up.

211
00:11:14,510 --> 00:11:18,090
Weren't you just telling Jin
how unsanitary carrying this is?

212
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:21,180
Sorry, it's not fresh.

213
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,770
[sizzling]

214
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:27,690
I'm your master now.

215
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,900
[grunts]

216
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:35,360
I'll be taking good care of you,
I promise.

217
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,990
[Asa grunts softly]

218
00:11:38,070 --> 00:11:40,660
Aw! They're more friendly
than I expected!

219
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:43,700
[grunts] I wonder
what their names are.

220
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:46,160
I've got you.

221
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:48,290
Save a little for later.

222
00:11:48,370 --> 00:11:49,460
We have time.

223
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:52,170
Though, why isn't
my brother here, too?

224
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:54,760
Did you see where he went
when I was trapped inside?

225
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,800
[grunts]

226
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,930
[Asa yelps] Spit him out!
Spit him out!

227
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:00,390
Let him go right now!

228
00:12:06,850 --> 00:12:08,060
[HARUO] They're out.

229
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,230
[ASA] Are you okay?

230
00:12:12,150 --> 00:12:15,190
[yelps] Slow down, there!
Those two are on our side now!

231
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:16,690
Explain it to me!

232
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:19,660
Uh, I used my Break power
to free those daemons

233
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:21,450
from their contract.
They're mine now!

234
00:12:21,530 --> 00:12:24,450
They have the ability to make
people vanish into thin air!

235
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:25,580
Do you understand?

236
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:28,710
Their old master might know
something about your parents!

237
00:12:30,210 --> 00:12:33,040
All we have to do now
is track them down.

238
00:12:33,130 --> 00:12:34,920
Great. But how?

239
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:38,550
[ASA] I have another request.

240
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:42,300
I want to know where
your previous master's hiding.

241
00:12:42,390 --> 00:12:43,510
Will you show me?

242
00:12:44,350 --> 00:12:45,560
[grunts]

243
00:12:45,850 --> 00:12:48,930
She's making a daemon pair
sell out their old master.

244
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:52,110
[SAKURAZAWA] Teenagers do get
scarier by the day, huh?

245
00:12:57,490 --> 00:13:00,280
[Hamura gasps]
Oh, come on, that's cheating!

246
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:03,070
I can't believe
they gave me up so quickly.

247
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:04,580
What stupid daemons!

248
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:06,910
Over there? It's too dark for...

249
00:13:07,330 --> 00:13:08,330
[grunting]

250
00:13:08,910 --> 00:13:10,910
-[Hamura screams]
-Hey, Right, mind grabbin' him?

251
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,080
I'm on it!

252
00:13:12,170 --> 00:13:15,460
[YURU] Good.
Anyone else out there?

253
00:13:15,540 --> 00:13:17,300
[ASA] Holy crap.

254
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:19,090
He grew into
such a good hunter.

255
00:13:19,170 --> 00:13:20,720
[cries]
I'm so proud of him!

256
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:26,810
What's wrong?

257
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:29,520
Apologies for all the noise.

258
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:32,020
As non-combatants,
please keep hidden.

259
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:34,730
We should have the situation
resolved shortly.

260
00:13:36,610 --> 00:13:38,030
[BOTH] Right.

261
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,400
[ASSASSIN] Yeah.

262
00:13:42,490 --> 00:13:46,660
Keep walkin', buddy.
We'll blow you sky high.

263
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,120
[screaming]

264
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:56,540
[grunting]

265
00:14:00,010 --> 00:14:01,670
[laughter]

266
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:05,390
[assassin gasps]

267
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:07,550
Good. That wasn't too hard.

268
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:12,980
Yet another face
I haven't seen before.

269
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:15,730
Hey, nice job, Jinny!

270
00:14:15,810 --> 00:14:18,440
I don't think any of these guys
were Kagemori.

271
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:20,820
The five pairs I've killed
have all been garbo.

272
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,280
Mine have also been "garbo."

273
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:24,360
For real?

274
00:14:24,450 --> 00:14:26,740
[assassin screams, grunts]

275
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:28,450
[groaning]

276
00:14:29,950 --> 00:14:31,500
[GABBY] Another fresh face.

277
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:33,540
[ASSASSIN]
No, no, no, no... [screams]

278
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:36,170
Don't kill me. Her dentures
already got my daemons!

279
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,750
I surrender!

280
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:40,250
Huh, who shot this?

281
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:42,510
I guess Yuru's back.

282
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:46,720
[GABBY]
I don't even see the lunatic.

283
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,570
[IVAN] Man, scary kid.

284
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:03,190
If I went out there,

285
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:06,700
I'd take one in the neck
before I ever got in range.

286
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:10,030
All our other guys have either
been captured or killed.

287
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,790
I think I'm gonna call it a day.

288
00:15:12,450 --> 00:15:14,160
I'm not one for pain.

289
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:16,330
Should've known
this group of nobodies

290
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:18,290
wouldn't have
a snowball's chance.

291
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:20,590
So I'm outta here.

292
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:26,220
What a joke.

293
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,930
Only bothered takin' this job
'cause the pay's good.

294
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:32,510
Now I'm stuck having
to scrounge up new daemons.

295
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:33,560
[grunts]

296
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:42,360
[whimpers]

297
00:15:52,870 --> 00:15:54,580
[gasps, grunts]

298
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,620
[thudding]

299
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,790
[bird cawing]

300
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:07,220
[birds chirping]

301
00:16:10,470 --> 00:16:13,390
[HARUO] Nice work
taking out the trash, Jin.

302
00:16:13,470 --> 00:16:16,350
[JIN] Yeah.
Awful lot of rodents this time.

303
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:18,730
You all right, kid?

304
00:16:18,810 --> 00:16:20,690
Sorry for involving you.

305
00:16:20,770 --> 00:16:23,110
You sure know
how to entertain your guests.

306
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,400
Thanks for the assist.

307
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:27,820
Don't get this twisted.
I am not on your side.

308
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:29,740
I only lent a hand
'cause it might help me

309
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:30,820
find my mom and dad.

310
00:16:31,870 --> 00:16:33,620
Asa, you good?

311
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:34,950
[gasps]

312
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:36,620
-[GABBY] Huh?
-[Gabriel growls]

313
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,290
Stupid brat.

314
00:16:38,370 --> 00:16:39,710
You little runt.

315
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:42,710
I may be small, but I bet you
I'm older than you.

316
00:16:42,790 --> 00:16:44,000
[YURU] Liar!

317
00:16:44,090 --> 00:16:46,130
[GABBY] Don't disrespect
your elders, son!

318
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:48,170
I let you walk away
with your life once.

319
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:50,800
Don't expect me to be so nice
if you cross me again.

320
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:53,510
Let's not start
another fight, guys.

321
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:57,310
Yuru and his guardians protected
this place by our side.

322
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:58,270
Yeah, no shit.

323
00:16:58,930 --> 00:17:02,020
Just look at 'em.
He caught a crap ton.

324
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:05,980
-[Right roars]
-[both scream]

325
00:17:06,070 --> 00:17:08,320
What should we do with 'em?

326
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:10,900
The master will decide
when he gets back to the manor.

327
00:17:10,990 --> 00:17:12,030
It isn't for me to say.

328
00:17:12,660 --> 00:17:15,160
Till then, let's ask them
some questions.

329
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,370
Talk to them, Haruo.

330
00:17:16,450 --> 00:17:17,660
I'm on it.

331
00:17:18,330 --> 00:17:19,830
[HAMURA] They offered me
a near fortune

332
00:17:19,910 --> 00:17:22,040
if I could just capture
some twin kids.

333
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:24,040
Got no name or face
I could give you,

334
00:17:24,130 --> 00:17:25,130
even if I were a snitch.

335
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:28,590
I think the old classic
should do the trick.

336
00:17:28,670 --> 00:17:29,630
[HAMURA] Hm?

337
00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:32,090
[HAMURA] Uh...

338
00:17:33,390 --> 00:17:37,010
[grunts]
Why is it so damn heavy?

339
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,430
[screaming]

340
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:41,180
Who reached out to you
about this job?

341
00:17:41,270 --> 00:17:42,850
Was it someone
from the Kagemori clan?

342
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:47,400
[screams] I swear to you,
I really don't know!

343
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:49,320
Please, stop it!

344
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,780
We're all just mercs!

345
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:52,490
I don't even know
any of the other people

346
00:17:52,570 --> 00:17:54,700
I was workin' with! [gasps]

347
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:56,030
I'm tellin' you!

348
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:58,330
We're just some
dime-a-dozen daemon wielders!

349
00:17:58,410 --> 00:18:00,040
Great, so you don't know
who hired you.

350
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,080
Surely you had someone
in charge on site?

351
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:03,750
The camo jacket.

352
00:18:03,830 --> 00:18:06,090
He had a camo jacket
and a beard.

353
00:18:06,170 --> 00:18:07,670
-He's in charge.
-[Akio gasps]

354
00:18:07,750 --> 00:18:10,050
[Hamura grunts, yells]

355
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,510
[AKIO] I think
I dealt with that one.

356
00:18:12,590 --> 00:18:14,340
I left him outside of the gate.

357
00:18:14,430 --> 00:18:15,890
My bad.

358
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:17,310
[Hamura continues grunting]

359
00:18:17,390 --> 00:18:19,060
Well, how about we move on?

360
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:21,270
We're looking
for a married couple

361
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:22,600
that fled Higashi.

362
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:23,810
What do you know?

363
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:26,360
They're these kids' parents.

364
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:27,940
They were
on their way to Okinawa

365
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:29,280
and vanished mid-flight.

366
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:31,030
No clue!

367
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,860
Now get this turtle off of me!

368
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:34,650
Think harder!

369
00:18:34,740 --> 00:18:36,120
We'll take anything you know!

370
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,780
[HAMURA]
And I told you I got nothin'!

371
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:42,080
-I'm clueless too.
-Same here.

372
00:18:42,160 --> 00:18:44,790
-Do you two know anything?
-[BOTH] Uh-uh.

373
00:18:46,290 --> 00:18:47,380
[Yuru grunts softly]

374
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:48,540
Then after all this,

375
00:18:48,630 --> 00:18:50,420
we're not any closer
to the truth.

376
00:18:51,050 --> 00:18:52,420
I know how you feel.

377
00:18:52,510 --> 00:18:55,760
Sorry your trip
was a waste of time.

378
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:57,010
[Yuru breathes shakily]

379
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,060
[Jin sighs]

380
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:01,970
Okay, last call.
Anyone else got a question?

381
00:19:02,350 --> 00:19:03,350
[ASA] Yes.

382
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:05,440
Mind answering one for me?

383
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,610
[HAMURA]
If you get this thing off me!

384
00:19:07,690 --> 00:19:09,980
Anything you want! Ask away!

385
00:19:10,610 --> 00:19:13,150
What are the names you gave
our little friends here?

386
00:19:13,230 --> 00:19:15,450
Their names? Huh? What?

387
00:19:15,530 --> 00:19:17,410
What did you call them?

388
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:19,910
[HAMURA] Why bother
calling them anything?

389
00:19:19,990 --> 00:19:22,950
If you're working with a daemon,
they deserve a name.

390
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:25,160
But they're like farm animals,
aren't they?

391
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:27,080
They're disobedient livestock,

392
00:19:27,170 --> 00:19:29,000
so you gotta beat 'em
into shape

393
00:19:29,090 --> 00:19:30,710
till they listen
to what you say.

394
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:33,880
Wouldn't name a mule
I used once. That's crazy.

395
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:37,300
[Gabriel growls]

396
00:19:43,270 --> 00:19:44,560
Easy there, Gabs.

397
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:54,940
[GABBY] I'm gonna go change.

398
00:19:57,990 --> 00:19:59,160
[YURU] Hm.

399
00:19:59,570 --> 00:20:01,160
There it is.

400
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:03,950
Now I see why your daemons
turned on you without a thought.

401
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:07,960
You know, we've got feelings
of our own, mister.

402
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,210
[Hamura whimpers]

403
00:20:09,830 --> 00:20:11,130
Got anything else to say?

404
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:12,920
Now's the time to cough it up.

405
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,260
-This was just some odd job!
-Same for me!

406
00:20:15,340 --> 00:20:17,630
And let the record show
my daemons have names!

407
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:18,970
[BOTH] Uh-huh.

408
00:20:19,050 --> 00:20:21,720
On that note, we can't
leave you without one.

409
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:23,010
So what to call you?

410
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,930
-[grunting softly]
-[laughs] Hey, cut it out!

411
00:20:26,020 --> 00:20:27,680
I'm only your temporary master,

412
00:20:27,770 --> 00:20:29,350
so don't get too attached to me!

413
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:31,520
You really are
quite affectionate.

414
00:20:31,610 --> 00:20:35,360
[grunts] Do you have
a smaller form, by chance?

415
00:20:37,990 --> 00:20:41,120
Oh, my gosh! You're so cute!

416
00:20:41,870 --> 00:20:42,950
Weren't you saying earlier

417
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:45,950
how assassins have been
hounding you day after day?

418
00:20:46,490 --> 00:20:49,160
Has your life been like that
since leaving the mountain?

419
00:20:49,250 --> 00:20:50,620
Sort of.

420
00:20:50,710 --> 00:20:52,840
But there were
so many this time around,

421
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:54,380
it seemed worse than usual.

422
00:20:56,590 --> 00:20:58,920
And having you here to help
meant a lot.

423
00:20:59,010 --> 00:21:00,010
Thank you.

424
00:21:04,220 --> 00:21:06,770
[ASA] The manor's been
a safe haven for so long,

425
00:21:06,850 --> 00:21:08,560
I stupidly let my guard down.

426
00:21:09,230 --> 00:21:10,770
I'll be more careful.

427
00:21:10,850 --> 00:21:12,520
[YURU]
If that's the way she thinks,

428
00:21:12,610 --> 00:21:14,060
it's no wonder she's jaded.

429
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:17,030
-[YURU] Hey.
-[ASA] Uh?

430
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:18,360
[YURU] Your eye.

431
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:20,490
Did they take that
from you, too?

432
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:31,210
[ASA] Well,
I suppose in a way, yes.

433
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,790
[YURU] Hm?

434
00:21:34,210 --> 00:21:36,130
[ASA] No, that's not right.

435
00:21:36,210 --> 00:21:38,340
I don't want
any lies between us.

436
00:21:42,550 --> 00:21:45,470
The truth is, I died once.

437
00:21:45,550 --> 00:21:46,720
[YURU] Huh?

438
00:21:48,020 --> 00:21:50,730
One of Higashi's assassins
killed me.

439
00:21:53,190 --> 00:21:54,900
[Yuru breathes shakily]

440
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:57,440
[♪ closing theme song playing]

441
00:23:27,990 --> 00:23:29,530
[YURU]
I could feel the hostility

442
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:31,740
through every pore on my body.

443
00:23:31,830 --> 00:23:33,330
Under my skin,

444
00:23:33,410 --> 00:23:36,920
stabbing straight through
my flesh and into my guts.
